hi my name is Aishwarya nya and i'm  working with Professor dan fry in the  mechanical engineering department so  despite the fact that there's over 1  million people who use wheelchairs in  the developing world there's very little  data about the usage patterns so what  we're trying to do is we're trying to  instrument several different types of  wheelchairs with sensors in order to get  long-term usage patterns across  different countries so we're using  accelerometers or using strain gauges  we're using wheel wheel rotation sensors  all in combination with something called  the sense in which is being developed at  MIT it's a data acquisition system that  will broadcast our signals back to a  central server and what we're hoping to  do with this data is first get real-time  user results over a month on period in  January in Indonesia then take those  results analyze them and see whether  there are improvement we improvements we  can make on wheelchairs but also see  what type of usage is happening in  different countries hopefully we'll be  able to take this and then put it across  several different types of wheelchairs  from a standard Hospital chair to the  LFC which was developed at MIT and then  maybe even make recommendations to  different users based on what their  needs may be
 

